{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And let nations bow down to you.</b> Even kingdoms that will not serve you shall bow down to you, so that you shall be supreme above the kings of the earth." "<b>Be a lord to your brothers.</b> For he thought it would be good for Jacob that the inheritance of the land of Israel be supplied to him and that he live in it with some subjugation, so that he not greatly exhaust his soul with material concerns and futile vanities, as happened to his seed afterward, as it says (Amos 6:8): מְתָאֵב אֲנִי אֶת גְּאוֹן יַעֲקֹב. And that it would be good for him to be subjugated under his brother, as they said, of blessed memory (Gittin 17): אִי בְּטוּלָךְ אִי בְּטוּלָא דְּבַר עֵשָׂו, because he knew that the land of Israel was fitting for Jacob alone. Therefore in this blessing that he intended to bestow upon Esau he made no mention of the blessing of Abraham or of the land of Israel, as he did for Jacob when he recognized him and blessed him." "<b>Those who curse you shall be cursed.</b> For wicked men curse their masters when they do not attain their desire; therefore he warned against this, saying: אֱלֹהִים לֹא תְקַלֵּל וגו׳ (Exodus 22:27)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:02.973241100Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}